# build artifacts and measurement outputs live under <home>/Research/<artifact-slug>/, never here
results/

# ONE scoped exception to the rule above, and only one. a design rule requires
# fixtures/broken-artifacts/ to be a COMMITTED tree of deliberately broken
# mini-artifacts; earlier plans commit .../results/figures.json inside it
# and an earlier plan's audit asserts that tree's committed count. Verified first-hand
# before this line existed: `git check-ignore -v
# fixtures/broken-artifacts/broken-unpinned-dependency/results/probe.json`
# resolved to `.gitignore:2:results/`, so those fixtures were silently never
# committable and the audit would have counted a population that excluded them.
#
# The files admitted here are deliberately-broken INPUTS to a checker, not
# measurement outputs, which is the whole reason the rule above exists. Every
# other `results/` path anywhere in this repository stays ignored --
# test_fixture_results_are_committable asserts BOTH directions, because a
# negation that admitted everything would satisfy the admission half and defeat
# the rule.
#
# The trailing slash is required, not cosmetic: git will not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY to find a negation for its contents, so the directory itself
# must be re-included.
#
# This does NOT relax a design rule -> a design rule. The fixture tree still sits outside anything
# conformance.py enumerates, which test_broken_fixture_tree_is_outside_the_scan_root
# asserts against conftest.SCAN_ROOT (an earlier plan reconciles that constant with
# tools/manifest.json.
!fixtures/broken-artifacts/**/results/

_pin/
*.env
.env*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The hash-pinned environment a design rule requires. A venv rather than the host
# interpreter is NOT a preference: `uv pip install --system` against this
# machine's C:\Python313 fails with "Access is denied (os error 5)" -- the host
# install is system-wide and needs elevation, so `.venv/` is the only place the
# `--require-hashes` install can land without asking for admin rights. It also
# puts the interpreter on a design rule's stated target (3.12.11) instead of the host's
# 3.13.5. The lock is tracked; the installed tree is not.
.venv/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Checker reports are written OUTSIDE the artifact and outside version control
# (a design rule: the checker must not mutate what it checks). This repository's own
# report directory follows the same rule -- every verify command earlier
# redirects into .reports/, and none of that output is evidence anyone should
# read from git history rather than by re-running the checker.
.reports/

# the publish script builds export trees here; they are rebuilt from the manifest
.export/
